<section id="A3.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.8 </span>Stability Analysis</h4>

<div id="A3.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct error analysis of VADTreeon UCF-Crime dataset and report their mean and variance. The randomness of the experimental results mainly comes from the randomness of the generated content during VLM and LLM inference. As shown in Table <a href="#A3.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ C.8 Stability Analysis ‣ Appendix C More Results ‣ VADTree: Explainable Training-Free Video Anomaly Detection via Hierarchical Granularity-Aware Tree ‣ VADTree: Explainable Training-Free Video Anomaly Detection via Hierarchical Granularity-Aware Tree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, the <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> across all configurations is statistically insignificant compared to the performance gaps between different methods (Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ VADTree: Explainable Training-Free Video Anomaly Detection via Hierarchical Granularity-Aware Tree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ VADTree: Explainable Training-Free Video Anomaly Detection via Hierarchical Granularity-Aware Tree" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). This confirms that the observed performance is robust against experimental randomness.</p>
</div>
